  "title": "Specializing morphism record",
  "description": "Morphism: a predicate-category -> the same with its specialization-pairs derived. Closes the declared specialization relation reflexively and transitively, verifies it is a partial order (antisymmetric), and checks that converse is specialization-monotone (p <= q implies p^op <= q^op). Specialization is the order along which a predicate refines to a more specific one; the reindexing along it carries the existential/universal adjoints.",
